{
    "word": "folkway",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c7b07a51-c275-3531-877f-2b37b58edbc4",
                "word": "folkway",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c088b77-84d4-4c4b-840d-a7c68865fa11",
                        "entry_id": "c7b07a51-c275-3531-877f-2b37b58edbc4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "folkways"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                        "entry_id": "c7b07a51-c275-3531-877f-2b37b58edbc4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Often plural: a belief or custom common to members of a culture or society."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2560a79a-5c81-4df7-acaf-4b70e17bcf0a",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "He [Van Wyck Brooks] had opposed to the folkways the standard of the humanistic life. It was needful that he continue to affirm that standard by making it visible in his own spiritual manner, by living boldly, dangerously, in the fashion of the artist, by giving himself to life as men in America had never dared give themselves. But it seems that for some reason he has shrunk from continuing the challenge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e61e6b03-5476-462c-8f6d-bb4898535523",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "By the time you are grown up and can consider the folk-ways of your childhood with detached impersonality, you have forgotten what was of most value. Rarely will a child tell frankly of his lore, and rarely can an adult remember."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec14a98e-31c1-4769-be79-e57a70dfd31a",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "[I]f he wishes to continue the memories of the past and his Jewish personality, the Jew must assume the obligations incumbent on the members of a national group. He must learn its language and literature, interest himself in the upbuilding of its home, and seek to adjust its traditions and folkways and religious thought to the wants of his time. Only in this way can the Jew maintain and perpetuate the Jewish personality."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22cc4191-7320-4109-b501-469e777dd676",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "For years I've hoped that some enterprising editor would hire a hillbilly to go to the city and write his impressions of the quaint folkways of the cliff dwellers. I'd do it myself, cheap, and I've got a good questionnaire tucked away in readiness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44387671-0fd9-486a-9e42-b09c9db91cc8",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "The restricted sustentive range of manipulations of foreign aid in economic warfare is especially marked. This is due to the state of the domestic law concerning foreign aid; \"reciprocal controls\" which a recipient state can exert; and a \"folk way\" expectation of economic aid flowing from centers of great productivity, such as the United States, the Soviet Union, and the countries of Western Europe. This folk-way expectation has emerged as a postulate of an obligation to supply the \"needs of the needy\" upon which foreign aid reasoning in both donor and recipient states tends to be founded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "272b977a-a98b-49db-bdad-59824c0bfa83",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "It [a social institution] is a folkway, always new yet ever old, directive and responsive, a spur to and a check upon change, a creature of means and a master of ends."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9643d68d-3616-497c-967b-24595e5080d4",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "At least since the time of Woodrow Wilson, studies of Congress have acknowledged the great importance of committee action in the legislative process. Stated in terms of legislative folkways, congressmen are expected to specialize in given subjects and then to rely on each other's specialized knowledge in areas that are not within their particular competence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85fea899-7d52-4122-a9a1-9ee22a83dd09",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "Francis Ford Coppola is not only engaged in making conceivable to the American audience the strange folkways of the Mafia, a process of translation of one signifying system into another. He is also using the difference of the Mafia to explore what the culture chooses to keep out of sight—the culture's preference for corporate values above individual/democratic and family values, and the Mafia's preference for family values not bound by the cash nexus but by blood, that is, values of the heart."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54b29cf6-57a5-4e5a-a36d-99d6f8913607",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "No one, reared in the folk ways of this particular subculture, growing up in it, understanding it, as he does, has spoken—not in its defense particularly, but from the 'inside.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f00623d-c8f3-46e2-9d8e-c21c1b901eb6",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "Avila was certainly well prepared to comment authoritatively on the folkways of his ancestors; he spoke fluent Quechua and had spent many years among the Peruvian Indians as a missionary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7b86d4d-1d2c-484b-991d-ee6e10863f4d",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "When rustic rites become cosmopolitan fashions, the artifice is often more interesting than the original folkway. Self-flagellation, for instance, is an unworthiness ritual in dirt road villages but a refined art form in the social sciences."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb4c4f92-1921-4d6b-ad7d-e4b0c94d7feb",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "From these supposed neolithic origins, the cult had declined with the advent of Christianity into a clandestine folk way practiced and handed down by a handful of individuals since medieval times, especially on the Welsh Marches, the place of its supposed prehistoric origin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d9f1ce9-1aec-4d96-a733-ba16d3d987fc",
                                "sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                                "text": "But what is at stake in the microscopic examination of folkways? Consider the following example: queuing at a checkout in supermarkets. The folkway governing this behavior could be summarized as \"First come, first served.\" [...] It's very likely that although the folkway (or social norm) \"First come, first served\" is used by shoppers to regulate their behavior, there are many circumstances in which it can be challenged."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3be1fccb-4c9c-4b37-b770-65bb68b1aa1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "c7b07a51-c275-3531-877f-2b37b58edbc4",
                        "source_sense_id": "eaef1c91-917e-3778-9f14-d4e6e550892b",
                        "source_sense_description": "custom or belief common to members of a society",
                        "target_lang_word": "Brauch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Brauch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                        "entry_id": "a2d52264-fb3c-3080-a281-c1fb23797bde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übliche oder traditionelle Verhaltensweise in einer Gesellschaft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6f12cd8-9c87-41d0-98c0-f115cbbb7cc2",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "Bei uns ist es Brauch, die Braut über die Schwelle zu tragen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6ffdf0e-60a3-4b0b-aaf3-dc96eabb9712",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "„Der Brauch soll auf das 16. Jahrhundert zurückgehen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1599cd7-93e9-4d56-8ac8-5ee9c9971944",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "„Dem Brauch gemäß eröffneten ihn Braut und Bräutigam mit einem Menuett.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29782488-fce0-47de-8fb9-8498448b7128",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "„Der Barkeeper muss zugeben, dass dies ein hübscher Brauch ist und lässt es dabei bewenden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96e5a366-3da2-4614-9072-bb17f01dbf58",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "„In manchen Kulturen ist es Brauch, als Teil des Bestattungsrituals die Gebeine der Vorfahren vom Muskelfleisch zu befreien und in seltenen Fällen zu verzehren.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bac46cb-5daf-4097-a153-f7eddbeda0db",
                                                "sense_id": "61cc446e-ad54-38b1-a899-2031eea61e03",
                                                "text": "„Als ich aus dem Norden nach Augsburg zog, musste ich mich an die bayerischen Bräuche erst gewöhnen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b090d21-314f-3009-a6b8-cdbe1d518fc1",
                                        "entry_id": "a2d52264-fb3c-3080-a281-c1fb23797bde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das Benutzen, Verwenden einer Sache zu ihrem Zweck, das Gebrauchen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "407c5c1b-178d-4fad-b37d-4ed8a4f7b9e4",
                                                "sense_id": "0b090d21-314f-3009-a6b8-cdbe1d518fc1",
                                                "text": "Man könnte meinen, der Brauch der Sprache verkommt immer mehr."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c10743b8-4113-4951-a78a-6e70e398b2e2",
